Kevin Cookson is the Scoutmaster of Troop 8010 in Yuma, Arizona,

18
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:04,899
And he wrote in to say this: my Scouts have achieved a new level of understanding the patrol method-

19
00:02:04,899 --> 00:02:09,199
Or maybe I'm the one who's finally figured something out.

20
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:15,600
I looked up an old blog post of yours dated September 26, 2012,- Troop leadership elections

21
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:19,400
And I went to our Tuesday night meeting and here's how it went.

22
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:22,600
The Scouts had known for months that elections were coming up.

23
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:26,500
I talked with my senior patrol leader about how he was going to run the elections,

24
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:30,900
explained what positions were elected, which were appointed, etc.

25
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:34,400
I told them they had 10 minutes and then I left the room.

26
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:38,700
That's simple. The new senior patrol leader came out, told me the results.

27
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:44,000
New patrols were formed and they had patrol leaders that even come up with new patrol names and yells.

28
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,700
I couldn't be more proud.

29
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:50,600
It's like you said: so much of the work of a Scoutmaster is really just getting out of the way.

30
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:53,700
With much gratitude for all you teach us Scouters.

31
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:56,299
Thanks so much, Kevin. I'm sure glad you let me know that.

32
00:02:56,299 --> 00:02:58,200
Yeah, get out of the way.

33
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:02,200
You know Scouts understand how to make things happen.

34
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:06,700
They don't make things happen in the same way that adults do, but they get the job done

35
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:10,299
and then they gain experience, they learn, they build character.

36
00:03:10,299 --> 00:03:11,500
What could be better?

